--    Section 2 via INSERT INTO storage.buckets. If your project blocks
--    that statement, create it by hand instead:
--       Storage -> New bucket -> name `vehicle-photos` -> Public OFF
--    Then re-run only Section 2's policy statements.
-- 2. The 190 JPEG files themselves are binary and are NOT in this SQL.
--    Copy them into the bucket under the same keys:
--    {vin}/photo-1.jpg ... {vin}/photo-5.jpg — public.vehicle_photos
--    already points at /api/public/vehicle-photos/{vin}/photo-N.jpg.
-- 3. Auth configuration: enable Email (Confirm email ON) and Google,
--    set Site URL, and allow-list /auth/callback and /reset-password.
-- 4. Passwords for legacy users who have not signed in yet are still only
--    in mycarco_db.mc_users as bcrypt hashes; the app's server-side
--    legacy-login flow migrates each account on first successful sign-in.
